  <p>If you click “Reject”, or make no choice, Google Analytics is not loaded and no measurement data is sent.</p>
  <p>No data is sold or used for advertising. In Google Analytics, Google signals and ads personalisation are turned off. Google Analytics 4 does not store your IP address.</p>

  <h2>Who receives your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> (Google Analytics), as a processor, only if you accepted. Data may be transferred to the United States to Google LLC, certified under the Data Privacy Framework (European Commission adequacy decision of 10 July 2023).</li>
    <li><strong>Cal.com, Inc.</strong>, 2261 Market Street #4382, San Francisco, CA 94114, United States, if you book a call. Cal.com processes booking data on my behalf, in the United States. Cal.com is certified under the Data Privacy Framework and also uses standard contractual clauses. On Cal.com’s own site, its privacy policy applies: <a href="https://cal.com/privacy">cal.com/privacy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>My calendar and email</strong>: the booking is added to my calendar <mark>[to fill in: Google or Microsoft]</mark>, and your emails arrive in a Microsoft (Outlook.com) mailbox.</li>
    <li><strong>GitHub, Inc.</strong>, 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. St., San Francisco, CA 94107, United States, the site’s host. GitHub logs visitors’ IP addresses for service security. Transfer outside the EU: <mark>[to confirm: GitHub’s Data Privacy Framework certification]</mark>.</li>
    <li><strong>LinkedIn</strong>, if you contact me there: LinkedIn’s privacy policy applies.</li>
