  <p>You can change your mind at any time with the <strong>“Manage cookies”</strong> link at the bottom of every page. Withdrawing consent is as easy as giving it, and deletes the Google Analytics cookies.</p>
  <p>The “Book a call” button takes you to Cal.com’s site, which applies its own cookie rules.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask to access, correct, erase or port your data, restrict its processing, or object to it. You can withdraw consent at any time, and set instructions for what happens to your data after your death. Write to <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. I reply within one month.</p>
  <p>If you believe your rights are not respected, you can complain to the CNIL, the French data protection authority: <a href="https://www.cnil.fr">cnil.fr</a>, 3 place de Fontenoy, TSA 80715, 75334 Paris Cedex 07, France.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>The site is served over HTTPS only. It asks you for no data directly: anything you send goes through Cal.com, email or LinkedIn.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>This policy may change. The last-updated date is at the top of the page.</p>
